  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [track-mode.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/f12a2f2b30ffd4e5ce1c5893e97e64af3c4675ba/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/track-mode.html#L4) test sets one source for a track element and then changes the mode a bunch of times. According to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#start-the-track-processing-model, this should cause a new fetch of the resource every time, leading to a load event each time the fetch completes. In reality, Firefox, Chrome, and Safari all have checks for whether the resource was already successfully loaded and skip fetching it, ensuring no events are dispatched:\n* https://searchfox.org/wubkat/rev/d221d71a6a560cb45bb3e9b23e526b6bcfa9e4b3/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLTrackElement.cpp#291-296\n* https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/b0bc20aac45f7cb55b18adbf4d2313457659d140/dom/media/webvtt/HTMLTrackElement.cpp#273-276\n* https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/blink.git/+/master/Source/core/html/HTMLTrackElement.cpp#191",
